-## v0.32.0: Race-only automatic driver
+## v0.33.0: Continuous adaptive corner targets
+
+Adaptive road-race speed now has a separate native planning command. Every valid sampled nonzero bend receives a smooth curvature-based target, instead of requiring it to cross the older curvature threshold. Exact straights keep the requested target ceiling; existing native lower/stop results are never increased. The native distance-based braking calculation uses the same pace compensation.
+
+The curve is deliberately conservative and experimental. It does not detect every corner on the map: the native planner may provide no corner records, skip a tail record, report zero curvature or use another route. It does not change steering, physical brakes, route lookahead, NOS or other cars. A hook hit is an observation of a past call, not proof the current corner is safe. Five fresh captures show hook hits despite reported missed turns, so the update is not presented as a proven fix for every failure.
+
+Only adaptive road mode uses this new command. **Street X and existing free-roam/road-corner controls retain their exact prior behavior.** The new command also denies actual/forced Street X and known online Street X in its native guards. AI ownership, native handback, online permission, mode checks and watchdog remain required. This does not bypass an AI failure or acquire control automatically.
+
+The option remains default-off/session-only and uses your current sliders without changing saved values. For the first comparison, try the existing defaults: 1.30× adaptive ceiling, 0.80 corner factor and 0.75 braking factor. Higher targets can still cause missed turns. The latest logs used 1.90×, 0.95 and 1.00 respectively; those settings were confirmed, not shown to be safe. Keep the working Street X setup unchanged.
+
+Corner/braking hit counters now use the existing two-second telemetry sample cadence instead of replacing bounded history every quarter second. Discrete control/mode changes still log promptly. No raw route geometry, memory dump or additional personal data is collected.
+
+Native tests execute the new corner and braking hooks against the pinned game routines, compare legacy commands byte-for-byte, and check protected outputs and guard denials. Live cornering, race results and browser rendering remain unverified. The final combined suite passes **1,942 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations**. All four supported patched modules compile, with only the two reviewed corner/braking wrapper functions changed from v0.32.
+
+## Retained v0.32.0: Race-only automatic driver
 
 In **AI driver**, enable **Race-only automatic driver** to arm the native driver for races you start or join yourself. It waits for the active race/GO state, includes Street X, Drag and Drift, and requests handback in free roam, outrun, results or other ineligible contexts. It does not find, join, start, replay or vote for events.
 
